      "id": 1,
      "text": "Johnson’s historic mill, first built in 1835, was burned in 1864, rebuilt in 1865, ran until 1985, and now houses the Inn at the Mill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/johnson_arkansas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Frisco Railroad arrived in 1881, sparking strawberry and grape farming, while the Crescent White Lime Company began mining in 1897, employing about 100 workers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/johnson_arkansas",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early 20th‑century Johnson hosted John Boswell’s 1904 barber shop, a long‑running blacksmith, a 1930s canning factory, and Upton Simpson’s 1951 truck body shop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/johnson_arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1886, and the community grew schools, churches, and small businesses before merging its school district with Fayetteville in 1949.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/johnson_arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Johnson sits in the Ozark Mountains, surrounded by valleys and natural springs that have shaped its early industry.",
